WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.600
Cobra Kai's third season has arrived and it
hit hard, fast, and with no mercy.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.280
Now that you've seen the credits roll, we're
here to ponder the questions it leaves us

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.070
with, from Aisha's possible return to Sam
and Miguel's uncertain future.

00:00:14.179 --> 00:00:18.949
In the finale of season three, Sam LaRusso
and Miguel Diaz convince the rest of the students

00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:22.369
from their respective karate dojos to sign
a sort of treaty.

00:00:22.369 --> 00:00:27.470
Essentially, they decide, whether their teachers
like it or not, to merge their two factions.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.240
While they agree to use the Miyagi-Do dojo
as their training ground, they haven't yet

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.410
settled on a name or a design.

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:37.650
Presumably, they won't be using those already
established by either dojo, and will create

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:40.120
a new identity for themselves instead.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:41.410
But what will that be, exactly?

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:46.370
A new name would certainly be appropriate,
as becoming one united dojo will likely require

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:51.910
a merging of Daniel LaRusso and Johnny Lawrence's
drastically different technical and educational

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:52.910
styles.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:56.680
While he's splintered off from the most brutal
aspects of Cobra Kai's philosophy, Johnny

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:00.480
still sees karate as a means to becoming a
hardened butt-kicker.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:04.650
Daniel LaRusso's karate, in tremendous contrast,
is all about balance and peace.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:09.630
Neither sensei is all that interested in compromise,
especially when it comes to each other.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:13.740
Moreover, on a purely technical level, these
are two totally different schools.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:20.030
LaRusso teaches Okinawan karate, while Lawrence
teaches Tang Soo Do, a Korean karate variant.

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:24.820
Whatever emerges from this union will be a
fusion of the two forms, and, by necessity,

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:26.190
something entirely new.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:30.000
Can the students learn each others' moves
while keeping their teachers on the same page?

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:36.120
The first season of Cobra Kai ends with the
climactic 2018 Under-18 All Valley Karate

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:40.659
Tournament, in which Miguel Diaz of Cobra
Kai defeats Robby Keene, then representing

00:01:40.659 --> 00:01:41.659
Miyagi-Do.

00:01:41.659 --> 00:01:45.830
A lot has changed since then, most notably
the fact that these fighters have switched

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:46.830
sides.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:50.229
Robby is now the presumed ace of Cobra Kai,
while Miguel is helping to lead the newly

00:01:50.229 --> 00:01:52.880
combined Miyagi-Do-Eagle Fang dojo.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.200
Now, the remaining factions have agreed to
resolve their rivalry once and for all at

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.020
the 51st Annual All Valley Tournament.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:03.830
During the last tournament, the make-up of
the finals was a foregone conclusion.

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:07.190
But going into season four, things are very
different indeed.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:11.590
There are enough prominent characters in contention
that there are absolutely no guarantees that

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:14.920
the next tournament will end with a rematch
between Diaz and Keene.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:19.370
There could even come a twist in which Cobra
Kai is eliminated in the semis, with the championship

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:23.340
match coming down to one of Daniel's students
facing off against one of Johnny's.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:28.360
Eli "Hawk" Moskowitz has been ride-or-die
for Cobra Kai ever since the first season

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.360
of the show.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.950
In the absence of Miguel, Hawk becomes the
dojo's top prospect early on in season three.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:38.310
Hawk gets less and less comfortable with Cobra
Kai throughout the season, however, as Kreese

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:43.450
gradually pushes out longtime allies and replaces
them with the likes of Kyler, the very bully

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:46.370
who Hawk joined Cobra Kai to defend himself
against.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:50.450
By the time the brawl at the LaRusso house
breaks out in the season finale, Hawk has

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:51.450
had enough.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:56.400
He turns against Cobra Kai, joining forces
with Demetri and the unified Miyagi-Do and

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.750
Eagle Fang dojo.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:02.200
Cobra Kai doesn't take kindly to traitors,
and one can imagine that they won't be waiting

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:07.020
until the tournament arrives to exact some
serious revenge against Hawk for his betrayal.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:11.930
Tory, the last remaining character from the
season two squad, is not exactly the forgiving

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:16.780
sort, while Kyler may very well resume his
favored pastime of menacing Hawk.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:17.830
"Traitors.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:21.239
You better watch your back."

00:03:21.239 --> 00:03:25.670
As Hawk was once the most zealous follower
of John Kreese's Cobra Kai philosophy, he

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:29.670
should have no illusions about what he can
expect from his old tribe, now that he's turned

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.209
decisively against them.

00:03:32.209 --> 00:03:36.730
In the original Karate Kid, Daniel LaRusso
finds himself constantly menaced by Johnny

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:38.810
Lawrence and his buddies in Cobra Kai.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:42.940
The feud begins to consume them, and eventually
even threatens their lives.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:47.900
So, after Mr. Miyagi breaks up a particularly
bloody and one-sided fight between Daniel

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:52.560
and five Cobra Kais, Miyagi and Kreese agree
to settle the conflict at the upcoming All

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.340
Valley Under-18 Karate Tournament.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:59.230
During the weeks between this fateful meeting
and the climactic tournament, the Cobras are

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:02.600
forbidden from picking fights with Daniel
at school, or anywhere else.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:07.810
At the end of Cobra Kai's third season, Daniel,
Johnny, and Kreese agree to use the upcoming

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:12.510
tournament to determine the fate of the Cobra
Kai dojo, but no other specific terms are

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:13.510
established.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:18.390
Given the all-out gang war that erupted between
Miyagi-Do and Cobra Kai this season, fans

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:19.390
are full of questions.

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:24.130
Will the dojos agree to a similar cessation
of hostilities, so that the students can focus

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.960
on preparing for the next tournament?

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:29.601
While such an agreement would likely deny
us a few of the fight sequences that make

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:33.889
the series so thrilling, it would help to
differentiate Cobra Kai's fourth season from

00:04:33.889 --> 00:04:37.749
its third, which is so thoroughly characterized
by its patterns of violence.

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:43.470
Season three expands John Kreese's backstory
tremendously, using flashbacks to reveal his

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:47.970
tragic youth and his traumatic capture in
the Vietnam War.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:50.909
In 1969, young Kreese saved the life of Silver,
a fellow soldier.

00:04:50.909 --> 00:04:55.099
Silver, who felt he owed Kreese his life,
fervently promised that he'd be there for

00:04:55.099 --> 00:04:56.569
Kreese for the rest of his life.

00:04:56.569 --> 00:05:00.789
In the finale of Cobra Kai's third season,
after present-day Kreese has agreed to stake

00:05:00.789 --> 00:05:05.789
his dojo on the tournament's outcome, he picks
up a photo of himself and Silver and places

00:05:05.789 --> 00:05:08.110
a phone call to his old friend and comrade.

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:12.710
Fans of The Karate Kid trilogy are already
familiar with Kreese's intensely loyal war

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:17.710
buddy Terry Silver: Alongside Kreese, he's
the antagonist of The Karate Kid Part III.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:22.240
There, Silver is a millionaire industrialist
who puts his entire life on hold to construct

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:26.710
a complicated revenge scheme against Daniel
LaRusso on Kreese's behalf.

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:30.789
It appears that Kreese is calling in a favor
from Silver — but what might that favor

00:05:30.789 --> 00:05:31.789
be?

00:05:31.789 --> 00:05:35.500
Silver is portrayed as a formidable fighter
in The Karate Kid Part III, and his money

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.749
could certainly come in handy as well.

00:05:37.749 --> 00:05:41.310
But Silver's greatest talent is for deception
and manipulation.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:44.699
Might Kreese use him as a fresh face to torment
unsuspecting students?

00:05:45.699 --> 00:05:50.460
By the end of Cobra Kai's third season, Miguel
Diaz and Sam LaRusso have reunited.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:54.699
This is a serious blow to Robby, who spends
most of the autumn in juvenile detention,

00:05:54.699 --> 00:05:59.050
then returns to Miyagi-Do to find that his
girlfriend has reconciled with her ex.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:01.999
"You two deserve each other."

00:06:01.999 --> 00:06:09.729
Now, as the show is concerned, they absolutely
do — but, you know, in a good way.

00:06:09.729 --> 00:06:13.539
Miguel and Sam have each grown a lot since
they were last a couple: Miguel has shed the

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:17.409
Cobra Kai skin that so hurt their relationship,
while Sam has come out the other side of a

00:06:17.409 --> 00:06:19.250
rage- and fear-fueled breakdown.

00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:23.590
They're both better, stronger, more considerate
people for having undergone these trials,

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:27.119
and are more able to bring out the best in
each other as a result.

00:06:27.119 --> 00:06:29.589
This is all very well and good for the two
lovebirds.

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:34.189
But Cobra Kai is, however, a big ol' karate
soap opera, which is just not the most stable

00:06:34.189 --> 00:06:37.330
ground upon which to build a healthy and lasting
relationship.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:41.770
History isn't on Miguel and Sam's side either:
So far, no romantic relationship between high

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:44.969
schoolers has survived an entire season of
Cobra Kai.

00:06:44.969 --> 00:06:48.990
Do Miguel and Sam have what it takes to make
it through what struggles lie ahead and survive

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:50.680
as a couple through the end of season four?

00:06:51.699 --> 00:06:56.319
Of all the regular cast members of Cobra Kai,
life has been hardest on Robby Keene and Tory

00:06:56.319 --> 00:06:57.319
Nichols.

00:06:57.319 --> 00:07:01.119
Robby has been effectively on his own for
years, with a deadbeat dad and an addict mom

00:07:01.119 --> 00:07:03.379
who is, thankfully, now in recovery.

00:07:03.379 --> 00:07:08.300
Tory's mother is on dialysis, and Tory works
two jobs to support her and her younger sibling.

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:12.949
They begin the season as bitter enemies, since
Tory is Sam's nemesis, and their rivalry is

00:07:12.949 --> 00:07:16.439
what led to Robby's own terrible mistake while
fighting Miguel.

00:07:16.439 --> 00:07:20.339
However, there are moments between them at
the probation office and later in Cobra Kai

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:24.809
where there seems to be an understanding between
them — and maybe even the spark of something

00:07:24.809 --> 00:07:25.809
more.

00:07:25.809 --> 00:07:29.949
Robby and Tory have more in common than just
rough childhoods: They've both benefited directly

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:32.000
from the Cobra Kai philosophy.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:37.009
Robby is routinely thrashed by fellow inmates
in juvenile detention until he abandons his

00:07:37.009 --> 00:07:41.309
Miyagi-Do scruples and stands up for himself
in a violent fashion.

00:07:41.309 --> 00:07:45.860
Tory would likely be at the mercy of her predatory
landlord if not for the personal intervention

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:47.240
of Kreese himself.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:51.129
Tory has been a true believer in the Cobra
Kai philosophy from the beginning, while Robby

00:07:51.129 --> 00:07:52.699
is a recent convert.

00:07:52.699 --> 00:07:56.619
All this, plus the fact that they're the two
remaining teenage leads at Cobra Kai, means

00:07:56.619 --> 00:07:59.999
there's a real chance they'll end up a couple
... at least for a little while.

00:08:00.999 --> 00:08:05.610
After roughly three seasons of will-they-won't-they
drama, Johnny and Carmen finally hook up in

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:09.039
the season three episode, "The Good, The Bad,
and The Badass."

00:08:09.039 --> 00:08:13.240
They both seem pretty pleased about this,
but are hesitant to commit to anything serious,

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:14.240
because of Miguel.

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:19.340
Johnny is Miguel's mentor and closest father-figure:
Getting serious with Carmen would mean wagering

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:21.449
one relationship on the others' success.

00:08:21.449 --> 00:08:25.490
What happens to Johnny and Miguel's bond if
Johnny and Carmen's doesn't work out?

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:29.789
The results could be disastrous — a fact
that weighs heavily upon Carmen and Johnny's

00:08:29.789 --> 00:08:30.789
minds.

00:08:30.789 --> 00:08:34.160
It appears as if Johnny might torpedo this
new romance right out of the gate when he

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:38.520
meets up with his old flame, Ali Mills, for
a very date-like afternoon and evening.

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:43.370
Selfies are taken, Golf N' Stuff is visited,
ice hockey is played, and a whole lot of emotionally

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:45.470
potent reminiscing takes place.

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:49.560
Thankfully, the night ends with Johnny and
Ali renewing their very-much-platonic friendship,

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:53.770
and the day seems to go by without anyone
seeing the two of them together and getting

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:54.970
the wrong idea.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:59.840
Johnny seems genuine in his interest in pursuing
a real and truly committed relationship with

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:02.030
Carmen, despite the risks it involves.

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:05.940
But of course, there are still plenty of ways
for Johnny to screw this up next season.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:11.010
During the first two seasons of Cobra Kai,
Aisha Robinson is a regular member of the

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:12.010
ensemble.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:16.280
In season one, Aisha goes from being the victim
of relentless bullying to one of the Cobra

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:18.650
Kai dojo's most promising students.

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:24.140
In season two, Aisha acts as the connective
tissue between Cobra Kai and Miyagi-Do, maintaining

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:26.780
friendships with members of both dojos.

00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:29.860
But in season three, Aisha doesn't appear
at all.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:33.590
Early in the season premiere, "Aftermath,"
it's revealed that Aisha's parents have not

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:38.190
only pulled her out of Cobra Kai, but out
of West Valley High entirely, enrolling her

00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:39.850
in a private school instead.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:43.320
The infamous rumble in the halls of the school
last season is to blame.

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:47.760
This is the only mention of Aisha in all of
season three, much to fans' dismay.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:51.860
This doesn't necessarily mean Aisha is gone
from the show for good, however, according

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:55.660
to series executive producer and co-showrunner
Jon Hurwitz.

00:09:55.660 --> 00:10:00.500
Before the season premiere, Hurwitz told TVLine
that Aisha may return in the future.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:01.690
Perhaps in season four?

00:10:02.690 --> 00:10:06.770
Cobra Kai has teased a rematch between Daniel
LaRusso and Johnny Lawrence since the show's

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:08.060
very first episode.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:11.390
The show is, after all, built around the pair's
infamous rivalry.

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:15.380
The two of them have come to blows only briefly
throughout the first three seasons of the

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:20.350
series: It happens once in season two's "No
Mercy" and is broken up by Sam and Robby,

00:10:20.350 --> 00:10:24.970
and again in season three's "Nature vs. Nurture,"
after they fight off a group of chop shop

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:27.540
tough guys together during their search for
Robby.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:30.871
Neither fight lasts very long, and they both
end in a draw.

00:10:30.871 --> 00:10:32.730
"Okay, you guys really like fighting each
other."

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.310
"He's instigating.

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:36.400
I'm just defending myself as usual."

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.450
"She knows firsthand that's bulls---."

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.800
By the end of the third season, their dojos
have combined.

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:46.060
Daniel and Johnny are now set to begin training
their students side-by-side, as partners.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:50.240
Tension between these legendary rivals is
at an all-time low, and apart from sparring

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:54.790
at the dojo, it doesn't seem like the two
will be going at it again any time soon.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:59.160
That said, we'll be disappointed if we don't
get one actual no-holds-barred LaRusso-Lawrence

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:01.360
rematch before the end of the series.

